AB  - Honghe Prefecture of Yunnan province is located in the subtropical humid monsoon climate zone of a plateau type in the low latitude. There are diversified climate types in this region with unique three-dimensional plateau type climate character. The current main crops (corn, capsicum, daisy, tobacco, etc.) here are not totally fitting in the regional natural precipitation, temperature and other climate variables. There are frequently great threats on the regional economic crops from the adverse climate. In order to make advance the transplanting period, growth process and harvest date of main economic crops in Honghe Prefecture, which can strengthen the drought resistance and water retention capacity of crops, help crops resisting the burst of disease and pests, reduce the impact of rainy season on harvest, and achieve the high quality and yield of crops, we studied the technology theory and method of seedling transplant in plastic mulch considering the principle of plastic film mulching cultivation and the physiological characteristics of main economic crops in Honghe prefecture. Based on the spatial-temporal analysis of regional ecological environment, our technology made full use of natural resources, such as light, temperature, water, fertilizer, soil, etc. Finally, the adaptive regionalization and the classified instruction of seedling transplant in plastic mulch in different region were achieved. The popularization and application of the theory and technique has significant effect on the development of modern precision agriculture in Honghe Prefecture. It also significantly increased the regional economic and ecological benefit and made good social results.
